From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:07:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bonito: stop starting netd from post-fs-data

The vendor rc started netd in post-fs-data, a boot-time optimisation from
when netd had no dependency on BPF. On Android 17 netd is 'disabled' in
netd.rc and started only by 'on property:bpf.progs_loaded=1', because
BpfHandler::init() aborts outright if the maps it needs are not pinned.

So this ran netd about six seconds before the loader, every boot:

  [44.964] starting service 'netd'              <- from here
  [45.027] processing action (load-bpf-programs)
  [45.160] Service 'netd' (pid 1572) SIGABRT

init then started it again from the proper trigger and it worked, which
is why this looked harmless. It was not: a SIGABRT and a tombstone per
boot, and netd's real start time was unchanged either way, so the
optimisation bought nothing.

The tell was that the second start ran netd then netd1shot, while the
trigger in netbpfload.rc does netd1shot then netd -- so the first start
could not have come from the trigger.

Verified: 1 netd start, 0 SIGABRT.
---
 init.hardware.rc | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/init.hardware.rc b/init.hardware.rc
index afa2788d..cbe836d6 100644
--- a/init.hardware.rc
+++ b/init.hardware.rc
@@ -239,8 +239,12 @@ on post-fs
     write /sys/module/drm/parameters/vblankoffdelay -1
 
 on post-fs-data
-    # We can start netd here before in is launched in common init.rc on zygote-start
-    start netd
+    # Do NOT start netd here. This was a boot-time optimisation from when netd had no dependency
+    # on BPF. On Android 17 netd is 'disabled' in netd.rc and is started only by
+    # 'on property:bpf.progs_loaded=1', because BpfHandler::init() aborts if the maps it needs are
+    # not pinned yet. Starting it from post-fs-data runs it about 6 seconds before the loader:
+    # netd takes SIGABRT, leaves a tombstone, and init starts it again from the proper trigger --
+    # so this bought nothing and cost a crash every boot.
 
     # b/38048356 Setup debug folders for camera
     mkdir /data/vendor/camera 0770 camera camera
